  "sampleScope": "Four source records from examples/authorized.mjs, one payload update, default finite read limits from docs/api.md. Work counters are trusted fixture diagnostics, not capacity measurements or public query fields. Reads stage zero writes by the read-only adapter contract.",
  "limitations": [
    "Fixture-policy enforcement does not authenticate actor identity; host getAuthority callbacks must obtain current policy within the transaction. No sessions, credentials, network boundary or revocation guarantee from immutable handles alone.",
    "Only serialized volatile memory storage is accepted; no crash durability, persistent adapter, distributed concurrency, original receipt recovery or production capacity acceptance.",
    "Authorized readers return records only; explicit anchor summary publication and cross-request continuation fencing remain JS-P4b.3/JS-P4c. No global visible rank, cross-model ordered union or global revision counter.",
    "Raw adapter/tree/writer functions remain privileged. New changed reference positions require Use; unchanged references and generated repairs retain separate integrity obligations.",
    "Owner streams use cached inorder paths and heap heads but may issue single-key batches. Source schema/projection cost, authority provider preparation, effective grant copying and callback CPU are not fully capped.",
    "Byte and physical scan limits are checked after fetch/clone/encoding or scan; memory incoming discovery enumerates the full store and sorts matches, even for small requested pages. No hard heap/transport cap or logarithmic whole-transaction claim.",
    "Work diagnostics may reveal hidden population and are passed only to a trusted callback. Timing and WORK_LIMIT behavior are not a noninterference guarantee.",
    "Traversal checks visited structure and hydrated candidates; independent checkStore remains necessary for full active-generation integrity. Inactive generations and lifecycle activation remain open.",
    "Index lifecycle, developer population/workload tools and bounded capacity demonstrations remain JS-P5; examples stay ordinary importable Node functions."
  ],
  "continuation": "Stop after committing and pushing JS-P4b.2 as requested. Next authorized continuation starts with the JS-P4b.3 summary-disclosure decision and JS-P4c continuation fencing; full P4 and JS-P5 remain open.",
